(301843, 21143, 5728, '<td valign="top">Thanx for all the comments. The textures in the blue rose come from the dying process at the florists. This was originally a white rose and which was placed in water with blue dye in it and slowly turned blue. It isnt possible to get a perfect blue though and this is the best which could be achieved. I also sprayed water on the roses to bring out the colors more. The effect seems a little oversaturated as some have said, however other than cropping and resizing I didnt post process them at all.</td>', 'Thanx for all the comments. The textures in the blue rose come from the dying process at the florists. This was originally a white rose and which was placed in water with blue dye in it and slowly turned blue. It isnt possible to get a perfect blue though and this is the best which could be achieved. I also sprayed water on the roses to bring out the colors more. The effect seems a little oversaturated as some have said, however other than cropping and resizing I didnt post process them at all.', '2003-05-19 04:18:32.000000', NULL, 0),
