(303004, 21089, 2923, '<td valign="top">I knew these were fake butterfly, hence the 2 vote, you can tell by looking at the perfect colors of the butterfly wings, which doesn''t happen in nature, also the edges of the wings, looks like it''s CUT from paper.<br/> <br/>We already have what, a ton of photos with hue adjustments and shifted colors FOR NATURE shots (which i consider blasphemous), but this one is worse.  It''s just like spot editing an image by inserting elements that weren''t there before.  I don''t care for other shots, but for nature shots I''d expect real photographs, not fake ones.<br/> <br/></td>', 'I knew these were fake butterfly, hence the 2 vote, you can tell by looking at the perfect colors of the butterfly wings, which doesn''t happen in nature, also the edges of the wings, looks like it''s CUT from paper. We already have what, a ton of photos with hue adjustments and shifted colors FOR NATURE shots (which i consider blasphemous), but this one is worse.  It''s just like spot editing an image by inserting elements that weren''t there before.  I don''t care for other shots, but for nature shots I''d expect real photographs, not fake ones. ', '2003-05-20 12:20:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(303007, 21089, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by paganini:</b></div><hr/><i>I knew these were fake butterfly, hence the 2 vote, you can tell by looking at the perfect colors of the butterfly wings, which doesn''t happen in nature, also the edges of the wings, looks like it''s CUT from paper.<br/> <br/>We already have what, a ton of photos with hue adjustments and shifted colors FOR NATURE shots (which i consider blasphemous), but this one is worse.  It''s just like spot editing an image by inserting elements that weren''t there before.  I don''t care for other shots, but for nature shots I''d expect real photographs, not fake ones.</i></td></tr></table> <br/>This wasn''t a "Nature" challenge, it was a COLOR challenge. I see it as a "real photograph" of a variety of objects in the colors specified...</td>', 'Originally posted by paganini:I knew these were fake butterfly, hence the 2 vote, you can tell by looking at the perfect colors of the butterfly wings, which doesn''t happen in nature, also the edges of the wings, looks like it''s CUT from paper. We already have what, a ton of photos with hue adjustments and shifted colors FOR NATURE shots (which i consider blasphemous), but this one is worse.  It''s just like spot editing an image by inserting elements that weren''t there before.  I don''t care for other shots, but for nature shots I''d expect real photographs, not fake ones. This wasn''t a "Nature" challenge, it was a COLOR challenge. I see it as a "real photograph" of a variety of objects in the colors specified...', '2003-05-20 12:37:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(303033, 21004, 4090, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone.  My 1st ribbon...its a great feeling.  Still smiling now.  Thanks again.</td>', 'Thanks everyone.  My 1st ribbon...its a great feeling.  Still smiling now.  Thanks again.', '2003-05-20 14:06:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(303282, 20998, 2716, '<td valign="top">Wow!  Thanks for all the great comments.  I received a few comments and e-mails asking me how I did this shot.  I posted a little "how-to" here:<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=25124" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">How I did Primary Glass</a></td>', 'Wow!  Thanks for all the great comments.  I received a few comments and e-mails asking me how I did this shot.  I posted a little "how-to" here: How I did Primary Glass', '2003-05-20 17:19:19.000000', NULL, 0),
