(306367, 21004, 2667, '<td valign="top">Ag, this photo really underscores the raw beauty of simplicity. Nicely done, and congrats on your first ribbon!</td>', 'Ag, this photo really underscores the raw beauty of simplicity. Nicely done, and congrats on your first ribbon!', '2003-05-25 12:14:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(306379, 21089, 2667, '<td valign="top">David, this is a great shot. And for the challenge it was almost too perfect. <br/> <br/>For what it''s worth, I never had a problem with it being a staged shot. This is just not a scene that happens in nature, but it can be created in the mind of the photographer! Congrats!</td>', 'David, this is a great shot. And for the challenge it was almost too perfect.  For what it''s worth, I never had a problem with it being a staged shot. This is just not a scene that happens in nature, but it can be created in the mind of the photographer! Congrats!', '2003-05-25 12:23:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(307892, 21146, 4159, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for your comments, especially Heather and John.  I didn''t think this shot would be wildly successful, just because it doesn''t sport the saturation that I knew would give the winners their edge in a color challenge.  The colors are admittedly a bit washed-out, but that wasn''t entirely unintentional...I wanted to give the impression of a laundry basket that was never empty, and always waiting there, and so I thought that evidence of overwashing might help that along (interestingly enough, the yellow shirt actually <i>is</i> that washed-out in real life - I''ve had it for years).  You''ve made me see things that I didn''t, though (and smell them - thanks, John) and I do appreciate your taking the time to comment.<br/> <br/>Martin</td>', 'Thank you all for your comments, especially Heather and John.  I didn''t think this shot would be wildly successful, just because it doesn''t sport the saturation that I knew would give the winners their edge in a color challenge.  The colors are admittedly a bit washed-out, but that wasn''t entirely unintentional...I wanted to give the impression of a laundry basket that was never empty, and always waiting there, and so I thought that evidence of overwashing might help that along (interestingly enough, the yellow shirt actually is that washed-out in real life - I''ve had it for years).  You''ve made me see things that I didn''t, though (and smell them - thanks, John) and I do appreciate your taking the time to comment. Martin', '2003-05-27 13:04:38.000000', NULL, 0),
